# Big binaries that must never reach the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and nothing here excluded jars — so building
# from a local working copy silently baked ~103MB of dead ThetaData jars
# (ThetaTerminalv3.jar + lib/*.jar) into the dashboard image. A VPS build from a
# git clone never hit it because they are gitignored, which is exactly why it
# went unnoticed. Theta is gone now and these are dead weight either way.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluding *.csv or eng.traineddata: the OCR data feeds
# /api/tpo-extract and some CSVs under data/ may be read at runtime. Excluding
# either on a guess is how you break a route nobody tests.
*.jar
isolate-*.log

# cbedge-v3 (dashboard v3) build artefacts. The Dockerfile runs its own
# `npm install` + build inside the image, so shipping the laptop's copies is
# pure context bloat — and a Windows-resolved node_modules can carry
# platform-specific binaries that do not run on the Linux build.
#
# Listed explicitly rather than as `**/node_modules`: a broad glob here would
# also change what reaches the image for app-vite, owner-vite, budget-vite and
# recipe-vite, and none of that has been tested.
cbedge-v3/node_modules
cbedge-v3/dist
cbedge-v3/dist-vela

# Client demo sites are served by their own nginx:alpine container (bind-mounted,
# see the demo-sites compose service) — keep client previews out of the
# dashboard image built by `COPY . .`.
demo-sites

# Build-context trim (2026-10-08). Every push sends the whole repo to the
# dashboard build (`COPY . .`), and that copy was taking ~30s. Everything below
# was checked: nothing in app/, components/, lib/, server-v2/, middleware.ts or
# next.config.js reads these at runtime (references are comments only).
#   - gex_strike_history.csv is 61MB on its own; the other root CSVs are
#     one-off research exports. NOT excluded: "ESU6 - 5 min - RTH.csv" (read by
#     server-v2/backfill-tpo-from-csv.js), data/, analyze/, "md files/" and the
#     CHANGELOG*.md files (the What's New / changelog pages read those).
#   - The research folders, archives and patches are laptop-only scratch.
gex_strike_history.csv
gex_preview_history.csv
gex_eod_history.csv
gex7420.csv
patterns_12h_*.csv
analyze_12h_patterns.py
Claude outputs
backtest-core-level
backtest-noise-momentum
Vanilla
_to_delete
outputs
owner-vite.tar.gz
mobile-build.bundle
*.patch
# Nested node_modules (e.g. app-vite/node_modules left over from running it on
# the VPS host). The Dockerfile always runs its own Linux npm install for
# app-vite, and a stray host copy can carry the wrong platform binaries (the
# same Windows-lockfile problem described in the Dockerfile).
app-vite/node_modules
app-vite/dist
